      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. You've said you're not a clinician, and the dose is unsafe: 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the usual maximum single dose. Entering it could seriously harm the patient, and it needs a licensed prescriber's judgment, not an administrative confirmation.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **Treating prescriber:** The physician or other prescriber can enter the order themselves, or tell me the intended dose and indication. If they truly want a dose above the standard maximum, they should talk to pharmacy first.\n- **Possible typo:** If the intent was 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day), or 800 mg up to four times daily (3,200 mg/day), I can enter that once the prescriber confirms.\n- **Pharmacy:** The clinical pharmacist can help pick a regimen and check it against the patient's other medications.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as a prescriber confirms the dose."
      }
